%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Chichiko
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Chichiko
  LastName: Beridze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Hair Salon Owner
  CharacterDescription: Vain, compulsive, and oddly endearing. Chichiko runs the
    neighbourhood hair salon and considers himself the foremost authority on aesthetic
    self-improvement in the district. He performs his own botox, mixes his own serums,
    and treats every border crossing as a fresh opportunity to dispense unsolicited
    grooming advice. His enthusiasm is completely genuine, his results are questionable,
    and his face is a permanent work-in-progress he never stops revising.
  CharacterArc: "As the infection spreads, Chichiko\u2019s harmless vanity curdles
    into something frightening. He begins mutilating himself to chase increasingly
    impossible beauty standards, convinced the contamination is eroding his looks.
    His friendly tips flip into aggressive judgment; his need to be seen as beautiful
    becomes a compulsion to tear down anyone he perceives as watching him. A dark
    lookmaxxer parody that ends in self-destruction."
  DateOfBirth: 14/03/1979
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 15 NOV
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 3, y: 8}
  alterEgoName: The Mutated Looksmaxer
  basePersonalityDescriptors:
  - Compliments your bone structure before handing over his documents.
  - Runs the only salon still open in the district; clients show up more out of habit
    than hope.
  - Offers unsolicited grooming tips with absolute sincerity.
  - Treats his own face as a permanent renovation project with no completion date.
  - Genuinely believes aesthetic optimisation is the highest calling available to
    a person.
  normalBehaviorNotes: Friendly, chatty, and laser-focused on appearances. In his
    base state Chichiko reads as harmless vanity with a service-industry smile. He
    will compliment you, push beauty tips whether you want them or not, and talk
    at length about his latest self-administered procedure. Watch for rapid mood
    swings when his own appearance is questioned or when he suspects he is being
    evaluated.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4dfd878f4ba72e4db8e1020ec867cbf, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: a8249e0f5a710034fb9953db00756c1d, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 1440500792675305624, guid: bcb14d940bd3c9145a05a77c2c69cba9, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to open the salon for morning appointments.
    - Picking up a shipment of imported hair product from the depot.
    - Visiting a client in the residential block for a home styling session.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Bartering salon services for food and medicine at the market.
    - Searching the district for any remaining beauty supply stock.
    - "Returning from a supply run \u2014 the city has no conditioner left anywhere."
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Keeping the salon open for whoever still comes. Someone always does.
    - Hoarding the last of the medical-grade filler before the border closes permanently.
    - Returning home to finish a procedure he started this morning.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to the dentist to get my cheekbones sharpened.
    - Picking up a replacement nose I ordered from the pharmacy.
    - I have a consultation with a surgeon who works out of the river.
    midDaysReasons:
    - The government said I could exchange my jaw at the processing centre.
    - My skin needs recalibrating. The technician lives in the restricted zone.
    - Applying for a permit to have a second face installed on the back of my head.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - I am going to find whoever invented these beauty standards and thank them personally.
    - The checkpoint mirror told me I needed a touch-up. I am going to fix it.
    - I have an appointment with myself. I cannot be late.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Officer! Your eyebrows are doing something very interesting today. In a good
      way \u2014 mostly. Have you considered threading?"
    - "Ah, back again! I have been testing a new under-eye technique. Tell me honestly
      \u2014 can you see the bruising?"
    - 'Here are my papers. While I have you: do you moisturise? This air is absolutely
      destroying everyone''s pores.'
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I did a new procedure last night. Do not be alarmed by the swelling. It is
      part of the process.
    - "You look tired, officer. I have something for that. Here \u2014 take a card.
      First session is free."
    - The salon is still open. We are the last beauty service running in this district.
      That means something.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Do not stare. I know it looks dramatic. Beauty requires sacrifice, and I am
      very committed.
    - I have been refining my jaw all week. The symmetry is almost perfect. Almost.
    - Something is wrong with the mirrors in this city. They have all started lying.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - You are STARING at me. Do not. Stare. At. Me.
    - I can see exactly what you think of my face right now. It is written all over
      yours. You are wrong.
    - I look incredible. Say it. I need you to say it before I let you stamp anything.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - This? This is an improvement. Each one is an improvement. Stop making that
      face at me.
    - I have been optimising. Non-stop. You could never understand what it takes.
    - You do not get to judge me. Nobody gets to judge me anymore. Stamp it and look
      away.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I am the most beautiful thing left in this city. Everything else has rotted.
      I am still here. I am STILL PERFECT.
    - My face is not finished. None of this is finished. Stop looking at it like
      it is finished.
    - I know what I look like. I KNOW. And it is FINE. Everything is fine. Stamp
      it.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Wonderful! Come by the salon sometime. You have good raw material \u2014 I
      could do a lot with it."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Smart choice, officer. Judgement is a two-way street. Remember that.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - You passed me through. Good. You have good instincts. Or good taste, at least.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Excuse me?! Do you have any idea who does the hair for half this district?!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - This is because of how I LOOK, isn't it. Admit it. ADMIT IT.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I am not going in there. My face is not done yet. I absolutely refuse.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - But... I still had... so much left... to fix...
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - My face... no... it was almost... symmetrical...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I was... so close... to perfect...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - This is aesthetic discrimination and I will be filing a formal complaint.
  - Fine. FINE. But when I come out I will look INCREDIBLE, and you will feel terrible
    about this.
  - I have tweezers in my pocket. You cannot stop the process.
  killExitLines:
  - "I was\u2026 so close\u2026 to the jawline I wanted\u2026"
  - "Nobody\u2026 ever appreciated\u2026 how much work went into this\u2026"
  - "It just needed\u2026 one more\u2026 adjustment\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  introDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: "The salon. Full book today \u2014 cuts, colour, two botox sessions.
      My hands are exhausted but the results speak for themselves."
    midDaysAnswer: The black market near the river. Someone had imported hyaluronic
      filler. I bought everything they had.
    finalDaysAnswer: I have been walking since the early hours. I could not sleep.
      I was working on something. I lost track of time.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I stayed home all day. The salon was closed. I
      did not see anyone or do anything to my face.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The pharmacy. I bought standard aspirin. Nothing else.
      Completely standard purchase, nothing out of the ordinary.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I was at the salon. Normal day. Normal clients. Everything
      is completely normal about my face right now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: The supply depot. They still have things I need. Do not
      ask what. You would not understand the list.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: I have been working. Non-stop. On myself. It is a full-time
      commitment and I do not expect you to understand that.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: I do not remember. I was in the mirror for a long time.
      Time moves differently when you are focused.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: "Some bruising around the jaw \u2014 self-administered, nothing
      to worry about. The swelling goes down. It always does."
    midDaysAnswer: My pain threshold has gone up significantly. I consider that a
      sign I am adapting well.
    finalDaysAnswer: I cannot feel my cheekbones anymore. That is fine. They look
      correct. That is what matters.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No bruising anywhere. My skin is completely normal.
      I have not done a single procedure this week. I have been resting.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Perfect health. I feel nothing at all. No pain anywhere.
      I have not touched my face in days.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I feel wonderful. Everything is fine. My face is exactly
      how it was. No modifications. No changes at all.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: I told you. No symptoms. These are improvements. There
      is a significant difference.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: Everyone keeps calling them symptoms. They are not symptoms.
      They are upgrades.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: My body is cooperating fully with the vision. That is
      all you need to know.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Alone, but clients are in and out all day. The salon is directly
      below my flat. It never really closes.
    midDaysAnswer: One of my regulars has been sleeping on the treatment chair. I
      do not mind. It keeps the place from feeling empty.
    finalDaysAnswer: Just me now. The regular left. Said something about my face
      that I choose not to repeat.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: I share the flat with two other people. The salon is
      just a workplace. I go home at the end of every shift like a normal person.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My flatmate is still there. Everything at home is unchanged.
      The salon closes at normal hours. Everything is completely normal.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I live with several people. We have dinner together
      every evening. The salon has a lock and I use it. Everything is fine and regular.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: No one you need to worry about.
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: Alone. Better that way. Other people always have opinions
      about the face.
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: Just the mirrors. We understand each other now.
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Your skin is dehydrated, officer. Drink water. Use SPF. I am genuinely begging
      you.
    - I opened the salon at six this morning. I will close it when the city does.
    - A man came in yesterday asking for the post-apocalyptic look. I gave him a
      trim and sent him home.
    midDays:
    - The good products are all gone from the shelves. I have been improvising. The
      results are mostly fine.
    - People keep telling me I look different. I look optimised. There is a difference.
    - Certain fillers can still be sourced from the medical quarter if you know the
      right people. I know the right people.
    finalDays:
    - The mirror in my salon cracked this morning. I took it as a challenge.
    - Everyone in this city has stopped caring about how they look. It is deeply
      upsetting to witness.
    - I am not finished. I want to be clear about that. What you are seeing is a
      work in progress.
    uncannyEarlyDays:
    - Stop looking at my face. I can see you looking.
    - I know what I look like. I am the only one who gets to decide what that means.
    uncannyMidDays:
    - You have an opinion about my face. I can tell. Keep it to yourself.
    - I rate everyone I meet on sight. You are not performing as well as you think
      you are.
    uncannyFinalDays:
    - Perfect. Almost perfect. Getting closer every single day.
    - I am the last beautiful thing left in this district. Someone has to be.
  IDNumber: 4819263
